  m_Name: Blade14
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Blade14
  description: The Blade14 is a tiny, thin-flat blade located at the middle-center-center
    of the jet engine, made of Blades2 material, tasked with compressing and accelerating
    the air flowing through the engine, with an interesting detail being its optimized
    shape for minimizing energy losses due to friction and maximizing airflow efficiency.
    Its small size and thin-flat shape enable it to operate efficiently at high speeds,
    making it a key component of the engine's compressor stage. By working in conjunction
    with other blades, Blade14 helps to achieve the high compression ratios required
    for efficient engine operation, thereby contributing to the engine's overall
    performance and efficiency.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
